Revert the thread pinning - not a change I was asked to make

Pinning ffsubsync's numeric libraries to one thread was an unrequested behaviour change. The
measurement behind it (4 threads per worker unpinned, 1 pinned) is real, but "the load average is
above the core count" was my inference, not a fault anyone reported, and four threads across four
workers is a legitimate choice for the person paying for the hardware.

Reverted: the environment pinning, its helper and the parameter that carried it. The plugin runs
ffsubsync exactly as it did before 1.1.0.31. The hung benchmark process that actually caused the
CPU spike was a leftover of mine on the server and needed no code at all.

Kept: <AssemblyVersion> and <FileVersion> expanding from <Version>. That is not a behaviour
change - it makes the version the interface prints true. It was stuck at 1.1.0.19, so the version
line added in 1.1.0.29 would have reported the wrong build.

Verified: no pinning symbols in the built DLL, one version string (1.1.0.32), harness ALL PASS.

Version 1.1.0.32.
